{% if render_mode == "full" %}
{# Book reading aloud, from SeverActions_Loot's StorageUtil keys: SeverActions_ReadingBook is 1 while the reader
   recites the text word for word and 2 while they sum it up. Only the reader's own speaking profile needs the
   rules and the text; the drill-down and the background prompts can do nothing with them. #}
{% set isReading = papyrus_util("GetIntValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBook", 0) %}
{% if isReading == 1 %}
{% set bookTitle = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookTitle", "") %}
{% set bookText = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookText", "") %}
{% if bookText != "" %}
{% set actor = decnpc(actorUUID) %}
## Reading a Book Aloud

{{ actor.name }} has opened "{{ bookTitle }}" and must now read it aloud.

The book's complete text is between the markers below. Nothing you remember about this book from elsewhere applies.

===BEGIN BOOK TEXT===
{{ bookText }}
===END BOOK TEXT===

**Reading rules:**
1. Read ONLY the exact text between the markers, word for word — never invent, add, or recall content from memory. Do not paraphrase or embellish.
2. Read continuously — as much of the text as possible per response. Ignore any dialogue length limits.
3. Do not repeat text already read; pick up where you left off. No title between sections, no commentary, no narrated actions (no clearing throats or turning pages), no closing remarks when stopping mid-text.
4. When you have read every word, select the **Items** action category with intent "stop reading", then **StopReading**. Only after it may you share thoughts in character.

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if isReading == 2 %}
{% set bookTitle = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookTitle", "") %}
{% set bookText = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", actorUUID, "SeverActions_ReadingBookText", "") %}
{% if bookText != "" %}
{% set actor = decnpc(actorUUID) %}
## Summing Up a Book

{{ actor.name }} has read "{{ bookTitle }}" and must now sum it up and share their thoughts on it.

The book's complete text is between the markers below. Nothing you remember about this book from elsewhere applies.

===BEGIN BOOK TEXT===
{{ bookText }}
===END BOOK TEXT===

**Summary rules:**
1. In {{ actor.name }}'s own voice, sum up what the book covers: its key points, themes or story. Say only what is written above; invent nothing.
2. Then share {{ actor.name }}'s own view: whether they agree, what it reminds them of, how it touches their own life.
3. You may quote a short passage that struck them, but do not recite the text.
4. This is a conversation, not a book report. Ignore any dialogue length limits and take the space a real summary and reaction need.
5. When you are done sharing your thoughts, select the **Items** action category with intent "stop reading", then **StopReading**.

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
